# Media, renders, logs, and scratch files stay local — the pipeline scaffolds
# a fresh video/ dir on every Actions run, it doesn't need past output in git.
*.mp4
*.mp3
*.wav
*.m4a
*.jpeg
*.jpg
*.png
*.log
*.txt.bak
__pycache__/
_kaggle_flux_kernel/
_kaggle_cog_kernel/

# Never commit real credentials.
*secrets*.json
pending_approvals.json
client_secret.json
refresh_token.txt
*.log
_listen_log.txt
_telegram_offset.txt
_deliver_log*.txt

# Comic-PDF/Gumroad workstream state — separate system, not part of the video
# pipeline; leave it out of this repo entirely rather than half-track it.
_captions_unresolved.json
_deliver_for_approval.py
_get_captions.py
_gumroad_publish.py
_telegram_listen.py
_telegram_send.py
state.py
_channel_videos*.json
_list_videos*.py
_youtube_auth_remint.py

# Keep the channel-wide reference bed and the dedup ledger even though the
# blanket media rules above would otherwise exclude them.
!_pipeline/assets/bed.wav
!_pipeline/cases_used.json

# 30-day batch pregen: local credentials never get committed. Every day's full
# asset set (narration, shots.json, meta.json, all 16 stills) DOES get
# committed — these are the actual deliverable, consumed later once a hook
# video comes back from Google Flow, possibly weeks after generation, so they
# can't be left to expire as a time-limited Actions artifact. Shot 1 also gets
# linked from the Google Sheet as a raw GitHub URL, since a personal-Gmail
# service account has no Drive storage quota of its own to host images under.
# Once a hook video/TTS narration are added (finishing a day for render), those
# also get committed into the same day dir — the render job runs on GitHub
# Actions (the only place this pipeline's heavy compositions render reliably;
# see render-performance notes), so it needs real access to these files, not
# just a local laptop path.
_pipeline/_local/
_pipeline/batch/*/_kaggle_flux_kernel/
_pipeline/batch/*/_kaggle_pixart_kernel/
!_pipeline/batch/**/*.jpeg
!_pipeline/batch/**/*.json
!_pipeline/batch/**/*.mp4
!_pipeline/batch/**/*.wav
!_pipeline/batch/**/*.html

# Per-video project directories (renders, generated images, transcripts) —
# not automation code, not needed in the repo.
*-short/
*-long/
_flux_noir_test/
_new/
